  "prefLabel": "Emab 201.01 Rules for Adjudicative Proceedings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Emab 201.01 Rules for Adjudicative Proceedings.\n\nThe appellate board’s review is confined to the record. The appellate board does not receive or consider evidence and therefore rules relative to adjudicative hearings are inapplicable. The proceedings before the appellate board are not those intended to be included under RSA 541-A:30-a.\n\nSource. #10394, eff 8-9-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/emab200.html"
}
